{
  "name": "Approval · 1 Request",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Approval · Request\nOpens an approval request and sends each approver their own link. Then this workflow is **finished**: nothing waits in a Wait node, the request is a row in the data table.\n\nCall it with `{ title, details, approvers: [\"Ana\", \"Ben\"], ttl_seconds, payload }` from an **Execute Sub-workflow** node or `POST approval/request`. `payload` is handed to the guarded action when someone approves.\n\n- The row starts as `pending` with `expires_at`.\n- The link in the message points at **Approval · 2 Decide** (`approval/open?id=...&t=...`), not at a resume URL. It stays answerable for as long as the row exists.\n- Replace **Send the request** with your Slack, mail or Teams node: one item per approver with `to`, `title`, `details`, `link`, `expires_at`.\n\n`GET approval/requests?request_id=...` or `?status=pending` lists rows, `GET approval/events?request_id=...` the log.",
        "width": 700,
        "height": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "f4aaf2e5-9b40-40c0-8718-ebe483b50da5",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "inputSource": "passthrough"
      },
      "id": "417047a6-53a4-4cd7-8083-87983695b389",
      "name": "When called",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
